## The reflexes to catch

Each of these was shown wrong about a hundred years ago. When one appears in an agent's reasoning it is an error
of the same kind as a type error, and it is removed, not weighed.

- A stage: a space or a time given in advance, on which things happen.
- An infinitely divisible quantity: a value with infinitely many digits, a field with independent values at
  infinitely many points, an integral down to zero distance.
- A property held in isolation: a state, an energy, a position that a system has by itself, relative to nothing.
- Deference to head count: the weight of a position measured by how many hold it.

