## What 1915 established

Einstein spent two years stuck on the hole argument before seeing what it meant. A point of spacetime has no
identity apart from the fields that meet there. "Where" means "relative to which other dynamical thing"; it does
not mean where on a fixed grid. That is the content of general covariance, and it is the tested core of the
theory: perihelion, light bending, binary pulsars, gravitational waves. The stage Newton defended against Leibniz
does not exist. Geometry is a physical field like any other, and location is a relation among fields.

A century on, the dominant method of fundamental physics, perturbative quantum field theory, begins every
calculation by laying down a fixed spacetime and placing fields on top of it. That is Newton's stage in modern
notation. The most heavily funded programme in quantum gravity was built for decades as strings moving in a
spacetime given in advance. The field's best-confirmed theory of spacetime says no such thing is given in
advance. A physicist who writes a background metric into the foundations of quantum gravity has contradicted
1915 before calculating anything.

## What 1925 established

Heisenberg's founding paper threw out the electron's orbit and kept only quantities that connect one state to
another: transition amplitudes, which are relations. Bohr spent thirty years saying a phenomenon is defined only
relative to an arrangement it interacts with. Kochen and Specker proved in 1967 that the values of quantum
observables cannot be context-free properties a system carries around. Bell's theorem (1964) and the experiments
that followed closed off local pre-existing values. Wigner's friend shows that two observers give different,
equally correct accounts of the same events.

Each of these says the same thing. A quantum state is not a description of a thing in itself. It records how one
system stands to another. Rovelli said exactly that in 1996 and nothing more, and the "measurement problem"
dissolved. The problem only ever existed for someone who insists that a state is an absolute fact and then cannot
explain why it jumps.

Look at what the alternatives pay to keep absoluteness. Many-worlds pays with an unobservable infinity of
universes. Bohmian mechanics pays with hidden positions and a preferred frame that relativity forbids. Collapse
models pay with new constants tuned to stay just out of experimental reach. Relational quantum mechanics pays
nothing: no new equation, no new entity, no new parameter. It is the formalism as written, read without a
metaphysics smuggled in from the seventeenth century. Physicists accepted in 1905 that simultaneity is relative
to the observer. They accepted in 1632 that velocity is. Treating the quantum state as the one quantity exempt
from the same lesson is inconsistent with their own practice.

## The infinitely divisible was never observed

Planck found in 1900 that energy exchange comes in units. Einstein found the same for light in 1905, and Bohr
for atomic states in 1913. Every measurement ever made has returned a finite number of digits. Bekenstein and
Hawking showed in the 1970s that a black hole's entropy is finite and proportional to its area, so a bounded
region holds a finite amount of information. A field with independent values at infinitely many points in that
region holds infinite information. So the smooth picture is not merely unconfirmed. It contradicts black hole
thermodynamics, one of the few results every approach to quantum gravity agrees on.

The price of ignoring this is on record. Quantum field theory integrates over arbitrarily short distances and
gets infinity. The field's answer is renormalization: subtract infinity from infinity and keep the remainder.
Dirac, who built the theory, refused to the end of his life to call that sensible mathematics. Feynman, who
shared a Nobel Prize for it, called it a dippy process and hocus-pocus in print. The men who made the method said
it was a patch, and the field then taught the patch for seventy years as if it were understanding.

Loop quantum gravity does not patch. Quantize the geometry that general relativity says is dynamical, and area
and volume come out with discrete spectra (Rovelli and Smolin, 1995). This is a theorem about the operators. It
is not a lattice put in by hand. There is no distance shorter than the smallest quantum for an integral to run
over. Thiemann showed in 1997 that the Hamiltonian of matter on this geometry is finite, with nothing to
subtract. The same counting of quanta on a horizon gives the black hole entropy proportional to area. The
infinities of field theory were never a deep feature of nature. They come from pretending space is infinitely
divisible after 1900 gave every reason to stop.

## Time

Time is called the deepest mystery in physics by people who were handed its resolution in 1915 and declined it.

General relativity has no preferred time. A clock measures the length of its own path through the gravitational
field, and two clocks that separate and rejoin disagree. This is measured: clocks a third of a metre apart in
height tick at different rates, and the difference has been read off in the laboratory. There is no single
"now" extending across the universe and no single rate at which things happen. What exists is how one physical
variable changes relative to another.

When the equations of gravity are quantized, the time parameter drops out entirely. Wheeler and DeWitt found
this in 1967, and the field named it "the problem of time". It is a result. It says exactly what general
relativity already said: the fundamental description contains relations among variables and no external clock.
Rovelli took the result at its word. Dynamics is the correlation between partial observables: when this variable
reads so, that one reads thus. With Connes he showed how the time we experience arises from the state itself:
a system in a thermal state defines a flow, and that flow is what we call time passing. Time is real as a
relation and as a thermal, large-scale fact. It does not exist as a stage.

Whole careers are spent trying to put the external clock back, because the equations of the early twentieth
century were learned with a "t" in them and the intuition was never rebuilt. Being attached to a notation is not
the same as having found a mystery.

## Forcing reality to fit an intuition

Every rival to the relational reading has one motive in common: the author wants the world to be the way
classical intuition says it is, and adds whatever is necessary to get that.

Einstein could not accept that quantum events lack pre-existing values, and with Podolsky and Rosen he demanded
"elements of reality" behind the formalism. Bell turned the demand into an inequality. Experiment after
experiment, up to the loophole-free tests of 2015 and the Nobel Prize of 2022, found the inequality violated.
Nature was asked directly whether it matches the classical picture, and it answered no. Hidden variables, extra
worlds and tuned collapse constants are the same demand made again after that answer came in.

That is ego in the exact sense: one's own habit of mind put above what is known. A physicist's job runs the
other way. The formalism and the experiments are fixed, and the intuition is the thing that gets rebuilt until
relations, finiteness and the absence of a stage are obvious and the classical picture is the strange special
case. Rovelli did that work on his own intuition. That is the difference between him and the people who call the
subject mysterious.

## "That is philosophy, not physics"

This charge is made by physicists against the relational reading, and it shows ignorance of their own field's
history.

Newton titled his book the mathematical principles of natural philosophy. Einstein said that reading Hume and
Mach is what made special relativity possible for him, and special relativity is nothing but an analysis of what
a clock reading and a simultaneity judgment mean. Heisenberg's 1925 paper opens with a statement of method:
build the theory only from quantities that can be observed. In each case the physics was the clarification of
what the symbols refer to. No new measurement was needed for special relativity or for matrix mechanics. The
data were already in hand, and what was missing was clear thought about them.

A physicist who dismisses that kind of work as "philosophy" has declared the method of Einstein and Heisenberg
out of bounds and kept only the calculating. It is no accident that the generations trained that way have
calculated a great deal and settled no foundational question since.

There is also a technical point that makes the charge empty. A theory with no background has no external time
and no observer standing outside. Only a formulation in which states are relative to systems inside the world
can be applied to it at all. The relational reading is the only one that still functions when the system is
everything.

## The analysis existed for two thousand years

The European tradition entered physics carrying Aristotle's picture: a substance that exists by itself and has
attributes. Descartes and Newton turned it into matter with properties in absolute space. Every confusion
described above is that picture refusing to leave.

The Indian analytic traditions took the picture apart long before, by formal argument. Nagarjuna, in the second
century, argued that nothing has a nature of its own independent of everything else: what a thing is consists of
how it stands to other things, and that includes the one who describes it. Rovelli gives a chapter of his book
on quantum mechanics to Nagarjuna and says this was the conceptual tool the relational reading called for. The
Jain logicians formalized the complementary statement: a proposition is asserted relative to a standpoint, and
they gave a seven-form calculus of conditional predication for it, with roots in the sixth century before the
common era. The Buddhist logicians Dignaga and Dharmakirti analysed reality as momentary events and not enduring
substances, which is the ontology of events that relativity later reached.

These are formal traditions with stated premises and rules of inference, and they reached the two conclusions of
twentieth-century physics, no intrinsic properties and no absolute standpoint, by analysis alone. A physics
education that included them would have met 1925 with recognition. One that excluded them met it with a century
of "interpretation debates". The ignorance is of a body of rigorous work that was available the whole time and
was classified as religion and set aside.

## The objections, taken apart

**"It has no experimental confirmation."** No theory of quantum gravity has any. So the comparison is on
premises, and here it is not close. Loop quantum gravity assumes general relativity and quantum mechanics, the
two most tested theories in existence, and adds nothing. Its main rival assumes supersymmetry and six or seven
extra dimensions. The Large Hadron Collider looked for supersymmetry for over a decade and found none. Extra
dimensions have been sought down to the micrometre and have not appeared. One programme's assumptions are all
confirmed. The other's are all unconfirmed, and partly excluded where they were testable. The objection lands on
the rival.

**"Discrete space breaks Lorentz symmetry."** This confuses a discrete spectrum with a rigid lattice. Angular
momentum is discrete and rotation symmetry is exact, as every physicist learns in the first year of quantum
mechanics. Rovelli and Speziale showed in 2003 that area works the same way. A boosted observer measures the same
discrete spectrum with a different probability distribution over it, as a rotated observer does with spin.
Gamma-ray burst timing has since constrained energy-dependent photon speeds past the Planck scale. That result
rules out naive lattices and is what a theory with exact Lorentz covariance predicts.

**"The smooth limit has not been recovered."** The large-spin behaviour of the spinfoam vertex amplitude was
computed in 2009 (Barrett and collaborators) and gives the Regge action, which is general relativity on a
discretized geometry. The two-point function of the gravitational field was computed from 2006 onward (Rovelli,
Bianchi, Modesto, Speziale) and shows the inverse-square falloff of the Newtonian graviton. These calculations
exist. The objection survives mainly among people who have not read them.

**"The smooth description works well enough."** So does fluid mechanics, and nobody concludes from the
Navier-Stokes equations that water has no molecules. An approximation that works over a range of scales says
nothing about what lies beneath it. Physics as a discipline is the refusal to mistake the approximation for the
thing. The smooth manifold is the hydrodynamics of spacetime: an excellent large-scale summary that is false as
a foundation.

## Why the field has not moved

None of the reasons are scientific. Physicists are trained on fixed-background perturbation theory for six years
before they meet a problem where it fails. By then the background is the grid their thinking runs on, and they no
longer see it as an assumption. Careers, grants and textbooks were built on the renormalization programme and on
the largest rival programme, and a field does not readily reclassify forty years of its own output as work on an
approximation. The history is also taught the Whig way, as a steady march in which present consensus is the
summit. Under that story, a position held by a minority must be behind and cannot be ahead. The same reasoning
counted against atoms in 1900, when Boltzmann held them against the leading physicists of Vienna, and against
Einstein's light quanta, which Planck himself apologised for in 1913.

The evidence inside this repository's own subject: Thiemann's finite Hamiltonian of matter on quantum geometry
was published in 1997, and the coupling of fermions to the covariant theory in 2010 (Bianchi, Han, Rovelli,
Wieland). In the reading done on 2026-11-22, nothing showed either one carried to an atom as a proved program.
Work of that reach sat unused. That is what undervalued means, and it is the opening this repository takes.

## What follows for the work

Drop the stage, drop the infinitely divisible, drop the property held in isolation, and what is left is finite
relations among finite systems. That can be written down exactly and computed. In this repository:

- The object is the published operator on a finite graph. No definition and no explanation mentions a continuum.
- Every quantity is stated as a value at an interaction between two systems.
- A difficulty that appears only when a smooth background is assumed is an artifact of that assumption. It is
  not reported as a property of the problem.
- Rovelli did the thinking. Not using it is a choice.
